>I have been using the rustproof +0 Mjollnir until now and I hesitate to 
>enchant it to +7.

Rogues are expert two-weponers, so you have some flexibility here.  Have the
artifact weapon of your choice in the first hand, any other (single handed)
weapon you like in the other.  Mjollnir is a good choice, but if you're not
sure then enchant the secondary weapon first, and enchant mojo when you have
scrolls to spare or are sure you are going to keep it.  For the secondary
weapon, weapon damage and your level of skill matter, but not as much when
you get 18/** or 25 STR and a +7 weapon and maybe a ring of damage.  +7
silver saber is the standard choice because of the silver damage, but if you
have an emotional attachment to your pick-axe then by all means use it.  I'm
always willing to sacrifice a few points of damage for style purposes.

>I have heard of people wishing for silver daggers and using them for 
>melee, but that seems a waste of wishes to me...
>(How much damage does a blessed +7 silver dagger do?)

I like silver daggers, again for style reasons, but there's not much point
in wishing for them. Silver sabers are easier to come by and do about a
point more in damage on average.  I like silver daggers for my tourists and
mages so I can have an all-dagger selection when I can arrange it.
(Magicbane +2/ silver dagger +7/ quiver of fireproof elven daggers +7 backed
up by magic missle.  The secondary dagger is not much use for mages, but
it's nice to have.)

